      "content": "Eddy Cue testified in US v. Google, the antitrust trial over Google's search business, defending the Information Services Agreement (ISA) which makes Google the default search engine on Apple devices.\n\nThe ISA has been in place since 2002. Cue negotiated the current iteration with Google CEO Sundar Pichai in 2016.\n\nDuring renegotiation, Apple wanted a higher percentage of revenue from users directed to the search engine, while Pichai wanted to keep the deal as is. They compromised on an undisclosed number.\n\nCue stated there was no valid alternative to Google at the time and there still isn't one. He argued Apple never seriously considered switching providers or building its own search product."
